 # UnderWeb X changelog
 
+## 0.5.6-rc15 — Bad news labels (synced) + UnderWeb sign-in
+
+- **Lobby Guard**: everyone in your instance is checked automatically against the shared, staff-reviewed labels (crashers, doxxers, malicious clients, harassers, scammers, ban evaders…) as they join. You get a private pop-up; nobody is kicked, blocked or told. Choose every label / caution and up / high risk only, or turn it off. Only VRChat user IDs are looked up.
+- Labeled people show on the Command overview ("1 labeled here"), in Safety Intel, and in the Groups tab's instance list.
+- Report anyone in your instance in two clicks ("Everyone else here → Report").
+- **UnderWeb sign-in in UWX** (System tab): email + code, the same as underweb.cloud. Never your VRChat login. The session is kept on this PC only.
+- **Staff (safety reviewers)**: publish a label for everyone straight from the report form, review the queue of reports from UWX and the website (approve with a public note, risk level and duration up to 1 year, or reject with a private reason), and remove labels. The server enforces who can do this.
+- Labels are synced through UnderWeb: once published, every UWX user sees them.
+
 ## 0.5.5-rc14 — Event Mode
 
 Command → **Event Mode**: pick an event type and press Start.
